&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Rare Opportunity to Shape the Future of Genomics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join a team of brilliant, passionate innovators determined to transform healthcare. At BillionToOne, we&#39;ve built a category-defining, publicly traded company on Nasdaq where transparency fuels trust, collaboration drives breakthroughs, and every contribution moves the needle on our mission to make life-changing diagnostics accessible to all. We don&#39;t just aim for incremental improvements; we build products that are 10x better than anything that exists today.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our scientists, engineers, sales executives, and visionaries are united by an unwavering commitment to changing the standard of care in prenatal and cancer diagnostics. This is where cutting-edge science meets human compassion, and every innovation you contribute helps remove the fear of the unknown from some of life&#39;s most critical medical moments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re driven by purpose, energized by innovation, and ready to help shape the future of precision medicine at scale, this is where you belong.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;Associate Director, Events Marketing&lt;/strong&gt;, you will lead the strategy, performance and evolution of BillionToOne’s event marketing function across national prenatal conferences, regional and local prenatal events, and strategic experiential activations. You will be responsible for defining how event marketing drives commercial growth, strengthens customer engagement, and advances the BillionToOne brand.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly cross-functional leadership role responsible for transforming event marketing into a scalable growth engine for the business. You will own the long-term vision for the event portfolio, investment strategy, pipeline generation, organizational design and operational excellence of the function. Success in this role requires balancing strategic leadership with strong operational rigor while building systems that consistently deliver exceptional results.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a strategic marketing leader with deep expertise in even marketing, demand generation and organizational leadership. You are equally comfortable shaping executive strategy, analyzing business performance, coaching teams and building the processes that allow organizations to scale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role may be remote or based out of our Menlo Park or Union City, CA offices and reports directly to the VP of Marketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Event Strategy &amp;amp; Portfolio Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the long-term vision and strategy for BillionToOne&#39;s prenatal event marketing function, ensuring national conferences, regional programs, and experiential marketing work together to drive commercial objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the annual event marketing strategy and investment plan, making data-driven recommendations on where the company should invest, expand, optimize, or reduce event spend based on business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define audience segmentation, event portfolio strategy, channel mix, and integrated marketing approaches that maximize pipeline generation and customer engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Executive Leadership, Sales, Product Marketing / Marketing and Medical Affairs to ensure event marketing supports company priorities and go-to-market objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Revenue Growth &amp;amp; Business Performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the event marketing function&#39;s contribution to pipeline generation, revenue, customer acquisition, and commercial performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish KPIs and performance frameworks tied to pipeline, conversion, attendance quality, ROI, and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze performance across the event portfolio to optimize resource allocation, improve return on investment, and guide future strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present executive-level business reviews and recommendations that influence marketing investment and commercial planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organizational Leadership &amp;amp; Team Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop prenatal events support, including full-time team members, contractors, agencies, and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build organizational capability through clear delegation models, defined ownership, standardized operating procedures, and scalable systems that enable the team to execute consistently at a high level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of accountability, proactive communication, operational excellence, and continuous improvement across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop talent, mentor team members, and create opportunities for professional growth while ensuring the function can scale with the company&#39;s continued expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership &amp;amp; Operational Excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish communication cadences, planning frameworks, ownership models, and governance processes that create clarity, transparency, and predictability across all event initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistent execution quality across executive-facing events, national conferences, regional meetings, webinars, and field programs by building scalable operating models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify organizational risks, resolve cross-functional challenges, and communicate mitigation plans with transparency and urgency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve operational processes, technology, vendor partnerships, and resource planning to increase efficiency and organizational effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Event Experience &amp;amp; Brand Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure BillionToOne delivers exceptional, differentiated event experiences that strengthen the company&#39;s brand, deepen customer relationships, and support commercial objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the strategic direction of flagship events while empowering the team to own day-to-day planning and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Brand and Design leaders to ensure a consistent, high-quality customer experience across every event touchpoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay ahead of industry trends, emerging event technologies, and innovative engagement strategies to continuously evolve BillionToOne&#39;s event marketing capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Marketing, Communications, Business, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8–10+ years of experience in event marketing, field marketing within the healthcare space.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning significant event marketing budgets and portfolio investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and business acumen with experience establishing KPIs, ROI frameworks, and executive reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing national conferences, regional events, experiential activations, and multi-channel event campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic thinking capabilities paired with exceptional operational and executional rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success partnering with Sales leadership to deliver measurable pipeline growth and commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence executive stakeholders and drive cross-functional decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence and communication skills with confidence presenting recommendations and influencing senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build scalable operational systems, improve cross-functional alignment, and lead through ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in fast-paced environments while proactively driving clarity, accountability, and momentum across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare, diagnostics, biotech, medtech, or life sciences experience strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, low-ego leader with strong relationship-building and cross-functional influence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits And Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working alongside brilliant, kind, passionate and dedicated colleagues, in an empowering environment, toward a global vision, striving for a future in which transformative molecular diagnostics can help millions of patients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open, transparent culture that includes weekly Town Hall meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to indirectly or directly change the lives of hundreds of thousands patients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multiple medical benefit options; employee premiums paid 100% of select plans, dependents covered up to 80%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extremely generous Family Bonding Leave for eligible employees (16 weeks, paid at 100%)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supplemental fertility benefits coverage&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement savings program including a 4% Company match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increase paid time off with increased tenure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Latest and greatest hardware (laptop, lab equipment, facilities)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily on-site lunches provided from top eateries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A variety of perks on campus (state of the art gym, restaurant)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free on-site EV charging (compatible with all EVs, including Tesla)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At BillionToOne, we are proud to offer a combination of a (1) base pay range (actual amount offered is based on experience and salary/equity options split that the candidate chooses), (2) generous equity options offering, (3) corporate bonus program, on top of (4) industry leading company benefits (free healthcare options, 401k match, very generous fully paid parental leave, etc.).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;BillionToOne is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For more information about how we protect your information, we encourage you to review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://billiontoone.com/privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BillionToOne is a next-generation molecular diagnostics company on a mission to make powerful, accurate diagnostic tests accessible to everyone. Our revolutionary QCT molecular counting technology enhances disease detection resolution by over a thousandfold using cell-free DNA,a breakthrough that has already transformed the lives of over half a million patients worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.unityscreen.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unity Complete™&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the only non-invasive prenatal screen capable of assessing fetal risk for both common recessive conditions and aneuploidies from a single maternal blood sample. &lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.unityscreen.com/webinars/confirm-gc&quot;&gt;Unity Confirm™&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;enables non-invasive confirmation for high-risk screening results through the capture of intact circulating fetal cells using BillionToOne’s Fetal Cell Capture™ Technology. &lt;br&gt;Our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.northstaronc.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Northstar®&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; liquid biopsy test uniquely combines treatment selection with real-time monitoring, giving oncologists unprecedented precision in cancer care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From $0 to $400M+ annualized revenue run-rate in just 6 years. In 2025, we completed one of the most successful IPOs for a medical diagnostics company, building on nearly $400M in private funding,including our $130M Series D in 2024 and backed by world-class investors including Hummingbird, Adams Street Partners, Neuberger Berman, Baillie Gifford, and Premji Invest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Recognition&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Forbes named us one of &lt;strong&gt;America&#39;s Best Startup Employers for 2025&lt;/strong&gt; and we&#39;re &lt;strong&gt;Great Place to Work certified&lt;/strong&gt;, with 100% of our people willing to go the extra mile, even as we&#39;ve scaled to over 700 employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Future&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Menlo Park with facilities in Union City, CA, and a new lab opening in Austin, TX in 2027, we&#39;re continuing to push the boundaries of what&#39;s possible in molecular diagnostics. We&#39;re just getting started.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to help us change the world, one molecule at a time? Learn more at&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.billiontoone.com&quot;&gt; billiontoone.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

