&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS degree in a scientific discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate II: 1+ years of experience servicing Liquid Handlers, or 2+ years experience in a technical service role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the basics of a coding language and flow control logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of clinical laboratory assays and their applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify, analyze and solve problems with minimal direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong willingness to learn in a complex laboratory environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent documentation skills with working knowledge of Good Document Practices (GDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills (verbal and written)&lt;/li&gt;
